            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 89-year-old male, admitted on 24/12/2020 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection (COVID-19). On admission, the patient presented with fever, dyspnoea, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest imaging confirmed bilateral COVID-19 pneumonia. Nasopharyngeal PCR testing was positive for SARS-CoV-2. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, dexamethasone, and low-molecular-weight heparin for thromboprophylaxis, alongside supportive measures including fluid management and physiotherapy. No intensive care admission was required. The patient showed gradual clinical improvement with stabilising oxygen requirements. He was discharged on 03/01/2021 in a recovering condition. We recommend continued monitoring of respiratory function, oxygen saturation, and general recovery in the community setting. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you require further information.</div>"
            },
